{"event_type":"review","id":"da670dd6fbee748a39ca5d51970b3e904bf175bd5582bc423467ae41448a06bc","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T06:44:14Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1af0e7b73b888d4a58bff92245141ade99129d58458cf7dd3ba90d46f3d06902","sha256":"1af0e7b73b888d4a58bff92245141ade99129d58458cf7dd3ba90d46f3d06902"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/f13d591b30cccbc4f2e4cd1fcec7a08da32e33d91449aba0dc55fc5538a10540","sha256":"f13d591b30cccbc4f2e4cd1fcec7a08da32e33d91449aba0dc55fc5538a10540"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b877ad59e0ab84fcf6621d772d1b78faa4196f2d812c2d79e632287042e0900b","sha256":"b877ad59e0ab84fcf6621d772d1b78faa4196f2d812c2d79e632287042e0900b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/01f1cc56646ed3964f3e98b738a3d9b353dcc6e42aa1f5e2ee5aa1d787f8ed8b","sha256":"01f1cc56646ed3964f3e98b738a3d9b353dcc6e42aa1f5e2ee5aa1d787f8ed8b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a4368dba714b7afe2bbc4b32cbdaeaf15e5d426ad3a3739a06383c64d9497c91","sha256":"a4368dba714b7afe2bbc4b32cbdaeaf15e5d426ad3a3739a06383c64d9497c91"}],"attempt_id":"491172ee4ef0bd48aa7a31f356abc230731f7ca77609b7358f1253691078df7f:0:1","base":"53257e8f8ff876bac1361fd2222d25b82fa27830","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"755e218dc85863461f5c58dddd19e7e1bf18b486","body":"**Write requests send no JSON reply when the deadline fires or the child process crashes**\n\n- **Where it fails:** `safe_handle` runs inside the forked child. Failures that happen in the parent escape `main`, and so do unexpected child exceptions.\n- **Deadline case:** `expired` raises `ValueError` in the parent while `supervised` waits.\n- **Child-crash case:** a `RuntimeError` from `crq.git`, a `KeyError`, or a non-`FileNotFoundError` `OSError` makes the child exit with code 2. `supervised` then raises `AuthorRefused(\"request refused; no permission\")` in the parent.\n- **Consequence:** In both cases nothing is written to stdout and a traceback goes to stderr. The client cannot tell a timeout apart from a refusal.\n- **Fix:** catch these in `main` and emit a typed `error(...)` reply.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        work = lambda runner: safe_handle(raw, runner, principal=principal, policy=policy)\n-        result = work(crq) if req[\"op\"] in (\"capabilities\", \"status\", \"result\") else supervised(work, crq)\n+        from author_quota import AuthorRefused\n+        def work(runner):\n+            return safe_handle(raw, runner, principal=principal, policy=policy)\n+        try:\n+            result = work(crq) if req[\"op\"] in (\"capabilities\", \"status\", \"result\") else supervised(work, crq)\n+        except (AuthorRefused, ValueError) as exc:\n+            result = error(\"unavailable\", f\"{exc}; retry the same request id\", True)\n         if result is None:\n```\n</details>\n\n`\"unavailable\"` is a placeholder code. Use a code that `operation.validate(\"response\", ...)` accepts.","id":"37cd2498d3a82fd72f56adb56935823a159bb3fccff34788aee0e5c4e3f5820b","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_transport.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Write requests send no JSON reply when the deadline fires or the child process crashes"},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"755e218dc85863461f5c58dddd19e7e1bf18b486","body":"**An error raised after `runner.save_queue(q)` replaces the success reply for an admission that is already saved**\n\n- **Where:** `review_transport.py:144` saves the admission. `local_review_runtime.prepare` then runs at `review_transport.py:148`, and only `runner.NotReady` is caught.\n- **What can fail in `prepare`:**\n  - It reads `meta.json` of an active PR run (`local_review_runtime.py:108`). A missing file raises `FileNotFoundError`.\n  - It calls `c.git` / `author_snapshot.git`, which raise `RuntimeError` / `AuthorRefused`.\n- **Consequence:** `safe_handle` turns these into `result-unavailable` (\"submit an explicit repeat\") or `snapshot-refused`. The item is already `created`, so an explicit repeat makes a duplicate generation and spends quota.\n- **Fix:** treat the reuse probe as best-effort and keep the `created` result when it fails.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n                 try:\n                     reused = local_review_runtime.prepare(runner, q, item, False) is None\n-                except runner.NotReady:\n+                except Exception:  # admission is persisted; reuse probe is best-effort\n                     reused = False\n```\n</details>","id":"b9ca10681c7faa16b5db45245debb8157ff71624944a31fdb2daef4d6f6e79a0","intervals":[],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_transport.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"An error raised after `runner.savequeue(q)` replaces the success reply for an admission that is already saved"}],"head":"4f92a6e0ab5d123506b03cf89b2cea8ee5f9c21f","head_tree":"1393f525755319d0614b0af7f33278d124294c49","input_scope":[{"blob":"2f42e410bf41e4536ae6a2308a014663def3a5ff","intervals":[[1,573]],"path":"apps/crq-python/crq_repair.py"},{"blob":"a56a5d61f8d126b8fa591b195c03cf45fcc10927","intervals":[[1,230]],"path":"apps/crq-python/local_review_runtime.py"},{"blob":"f08beb430844f6f60247147b26ca872b5d78b0a9","intervals":[[1,125]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_admission.py"},{"blob":"755e218dc85863461f5c58dddd19e7e1bf18b486","intervals":[[1,222]],"path":"apps/crq-python/review_transport.py"},{"blob":"16c673385986f94144f4765efc5deeba251f5ffb","intervals":[[1,193]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_local_review_pr.py"},{"blob":"56798197f92e59d4973d7a4384076cb0540f300d","intervals":[[1,462]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_queue_transport_review.py"},{"blob":"74b3fc40b